Author: Rob Eden <rob@robeden.com>
Date:   Wed Feb 17 18:01:35 2021 -0600

    Additional module-related test cases and logic fixes

    Protection against processing directories multiple times previously prevented correctly loading module data in some situations. This would lead to some oddly non-deterministic results, depending on directory traversal order. The two new test cases illustrated this with the old logic. Now the protection has been tweaked for module loading to a more precise method using the source and module reference index, which matches what is used in the `__resolved__` field.

